<launch>
    <!-- ====================================================================
         Carolus — rviz visualization, added 2026-08-14.

         Genuinely different from the launcher's own CAM PREVIEW / BLOB VIEW
         panels: those show flat 2D images (carolus_launcher.py, shortcuts/).
         This shows the actual 3D pose Carolus computes — the
         camera_link -> beacon_observed TF frame (published by T4,
         carolus_tf_broadcaster.py) — in a real 3D scene, alongside the same
         two image topics for reference.

         Needs T2 (camera), T3 (carolus_astrobee, publishes /postprocessed/image
         and /pose), and T4 (carolus_tf_broadcaster.py, publishes the TF) already
         running — this launches only rviz itself.

         Run on the lab PC:
             roslaunch carolus_node carolus_rviz.launch

         Known limitation: no camera_info topic is published by rm_cam_beacon.py,
         so rviz's "Camera" display type (which overlays TF onto the live image,
         and needs an image+camera_info pair) cannot be used here — only the
         plain "Image" display type, and a separate 3D "TF" display. The 3D
         beacon frame and the camera image are both visible, just not fused
         into one overlaid view.
         ==================================================================== -->

    <node name="carolus_rviz" pkg="rviz" type="rviz"
          args="-d $(find carolus_node)/rviz/carolus.rviz"
          output="screen" />

</launch>
